# Local dev fallback for the API base URL.
#
# In production, the API base URL is published at runtime as /config.json
# (written by CDK at deploy time, e.g. { "apiUrl": "https://xxxx.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com" }).
# The app fetches that file on startup and uses it for all API calls.
#
# During local development (`npm run dev`) there is no /config.json being served,
# so the app falls back to this env var instead. Point it at a deployed API
# (or a local API server) to iterate on the frontend without needing a local backend.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in a real value:
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Do not include a trailing slash.
VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-id.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
